{
  "name": "grip-upper-arm",
  "description": "GRIP's upper arm (github.com/connorwhite-online/grip, SLS edition), rebuilt generatively from its interfaces: the J2 shoulder hub with its four M3 bolts and the hex-driver access that runs through the link to them, the J3 elbow socket that seats the 25:1 cycloidal drive (sleeve and ledge), the NEMA 17 motor and its CAN driver hanging below it, the cable run, and clearance for the forearm swinging past the elbow. Loads: the arm reaching horizontally with 1 kg at the gripper (distal weight about 3.3 kg x 1.5, plus the J3 holding torque), the J3 motor stalling (0.65 N\u00b7m x 25 = 16 N\u00b7m), and a 20 N push along the joint axis. Goal: no softer at the elbow than the original (0.54 mm in the reach case, its own verified number under the same loads) with a safety factor of 2 in every case, as light as possible. The original verifies at 214 g with a safety factor of 0.54 under the stall case.",
